<title>SWEDEN: AGA posts 14 pct drop in 9 mo profit.</title>
<headline>AGA posts 14 pct drop in 9 mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish gas company AGA results for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  1,382 vs  1,602</p>
<p> Turnover				    9,523 vs 10,072</p>
<p> Earnings per share after tax(SKR)    4.04 vs   4.68</p>
<p> Operating costs			   7,311 vs  7,608</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,013 vs    977</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,199 vs  1,487</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CREDIT   164 vs     61   CHARGE</p>
<p> Share of income in Gullspangs Kraft   n/a vs    150</p>
<p> Associate interests, other		 19 vs     26</p>
<p> Cap gain on share sales		 1,794 vs    601</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    3,176 vs  2,203</p>
<p> Tax paid					486 vs    314</p>
<p> Deferred tax				  104 vs    166</p>
<p> Minority interests			    7 vs	9</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,579 vs  1,714</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Swedish industrial gas producer AGA AB. Analysts polled by Reuters expected a profit after financial items of 1.42 billion crowns for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
